.TH HYPRWAYLAND-SCANNER 1 "hyprwayland-scanner" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hyprwayland-scanner - generate C++ Wayland protocol bindings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hyprwayland-scanner
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " PROTOCOL_XML OUTPUT_DIRECTORY"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hyprwayland-scanner
generates C++ bindings for Wayland protocols, for either servers or clients.

By default, hyprwayland-scanner generates server-side code. Generated files are
written to the specified output directory.

A compiler with C++23 support as well as
.B pugixml
are required.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I PROTOCOL_XML
Path to the Wayland protocol XML file.
.TP
.I OUTPUT_DIRECTORY
Path to the directory where generated files will be written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -c ", " --client
Generate client-side code instead of server-side code.
.TP
.B --wayland-enums
Use Wayland-style enum naming.
.TP
.B --no-interfaces
Do not generate
.B wl_interface
and related interface metadata.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Print the program version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
The program writes generated C++ source files to
.IR OUTPUT_DIRECTORY .
Typically this includes a header file and a source file derived from the input XML filename.

.SH EXAMPLES
Generate server-side bindings:
.PP
.nf
hyprwayland-scanner /path/to/protocol.xml ./generated
.fi
.PP
Generate client-side bindings:
.PP
.nf
hyprwayland-scanner --client /path/to/protocol.xml ./generated
.fi
.PP
Generate client-side bindings with Wayland enum naming:
.PP
.nf
hyprwayland-scanner --client --wayland-enums /path/to/protocol.xml ./generated
.fi
